WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.762
Breaks are part of the job for your team.

00:00:03.762 --> 00:00:06.357
They protect well-being, and they protect pay.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:11.532
A rest break is 10 minutes, paid, in every 4 hours of work.

00:00:11.532 --> 00:00:16.718
It is already inside hours worked, so employees do not enter it on the timecard.

00:00:16.718 --> 00:00:19.376
A rest break cannot be skipped or banked.

00:00:20.726 --> 00:00:23.846
Unpaid meal breaks follow the work-location state.

00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:32.332
At this time, employees must receive 30 minutes or more once they have worked 5 hours, and a second meal break after more than 10 hours.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:39.757
During a meal they must be completely relieved of duty and allowed to leave the premises, or that time is hours worked.

00:00:39.757 --> 00:00:42.315
A meal break cannot be skipped or banked.

00:00:43.665 --> 00:00:51.604
If an employee is involuntarily prevented from taking a meal break, they enter the hours as one continuous block, with no gap.

00:00:51.604 --> 00:00:55.825
Workday then generates the meal-break payment on the next paycheck.

00:00:57.175 --> 00:01:02.765
For a missed rest break, the employee gives you the Notice of Involuntarily Missed Rest Break form.
